  "executive_briefing": "The digital asset market is currently undergoing a structural transformation characterized by the legislative maturation of the CLARITY Act and a fundamental shift in cross-chain architecture. The CLARITY Act (H.R. 3633), which entered Senate consideration in May 2026 after a decisive House victory, is providing the jurisdictional certainty necessary for Bitcoin to transition from a passive reserve to a programmable smart-contract layer. This regulatory tailwind is synchronized with a massive institutional pivot toward a dual-asset (BTC/ETH) treasury model, projected to capture up to 7% of circulating supply through ETFs and pension fund integration. Architecturally, the market is aggressively phasing out 'wrapped' asset dependencies (like wBTC) in favor of native-to-native liquidity protocols such as Symbiosis and Cobo, which facilitate trustless interaction between Bitcoin's emerging L2 ecosystems and established EVM networks.",
